From: Patch Generator
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2025
Subject: [PATCH] Remove QEMU trace infrastructure

This patch removes the unused QEMU trace infrastructure from the
vfu-rdma project. The trace headers were already stubbed out (empty),
so all trace_*() calls were no-ops. This simplifies the codebase by:

1. Removing all #include "trace.h" directives
2. Removing all trace_*() function calls
3. Deleting trace-events definition files
4. Deleting empty trace header files
5. Adding optional RDMA_DEBUG macro for development tracing

The existing rdma_error_report/warn_report/info_report macros remain
available for important logging.

Signed-off-by: Code Review Assistant <assistant@cursor.sh>
